# Data Models and Database Guide

## Core Data Models Overview

### Company Information ([models.py](mdc:data_hall/models.py))

#### CompanyInfo (Primary Entity)
```python
# Key fields in CompanyInfo model:
keyno = models.CharField(primary_key=True)  # Unique identifier
company_name = models.CharField(max_length=128)  # Company name
company_birth = models.CharField(max_length=20)  # Establishment year
insured_num = models.CharField(max_length=20)  # Number of insured employees
latitude/longitude = models.CharField()  # Geographic coordinates
industry/industry_sub = models.CharField()  # Industry classification
province/city/county = models.CharField()  # Administrative location
company_scale = models.CharField()  # Company size/scale
```

#### CompanyRanking (Performance Metrics)
```python
# Five-dimensional ranking system:
dev_potential = models.DecimalField()  # Development potential (0-100)
expansion_speed = models.DecimalField()  # Expansion speed (0-100)  
innovation = models.DecimalField()  # Innovation capability (0-100)
capital_attention = models.DecimalField()  # Capital attention (0-100)
team_background = models.DecimalField()  # Team background (0-100)
comprehensive_score = models.DecimalField()  # Auto-calculated average
rank = models.PositiveIntegerField()  # Overall ranking position
```

#### CompanyFinancing (Investment History)
```python
# Tracks company funding rounds:
financing_round = models.CharField()  # Round type (A, B, C, IPO, etc.)
financing_amount = models.CharField()  # Amount raised
financing_date = models.DateField()  # Investment date
investor_id/investor_name = models.CharField()  # Investor information
```

### Industry Chain Structure

#### IndustryChain (Top Level)
```python
name = models.CharField(max_length=255, unique=True)  # Chain name
code = models.CharField(max_length=20, unique=True)  # Chain code (IC0076)
description = models.TextField()  # Chain description
```

#### ChainPoint (Chain Nodes) 
```python
name = models.CharField(max_length=255)  # Node name
code = models.CharField(max_length=20, unique=True)  # Node code (IC0076001)
level = models.CharField(max_length=255)  # Hierarchical level
parent = models.ForeignKey('self')  # Self-referencing for hierarchy
industry_chain = models.ForeignKey(IndustryChain)  # Parent chain
```

#### ChainPointCompany (Many-to-Many Relationship)
```python
chain_point = models.ForeignKey(ChainPoint)  # Chain node
company = models.ForeignKey(CompanyInfo)  # Associated company
# Creates many-to-many relationship between companies and chain points
```

### Geographic Hierarchy

#### Province/City/District Models
```python
# Three-level administrative division:
Province: code (PK), name
City: code (PK), name, province (FK)
District: code (PK), name, city (FK)

# Enables geographic filtering and analysis
```

## Data Relationships and Queries

### Key Relationships
```python
# Company to Rankings (One-to-One)
company.ranking  # Access ranking data
ranking.company  # Access company from ranking

# Company to Financing (One-to-Many)  
company.financings.all()  # All financing rounds
financing.company  # Parent company

# Industry Chain Hierarchy (Self-referencing)
chain_point.children.all()  # Child nodes
chain_point.parent  # Parent node
industry_chain.chain_points.all()  # All nodes in chain

# Geographic Hierarchy
province.cities.all()  # Cities in province
city.districts.all()  # Districts in city
```

### Common Query Patterns
```python
# Get companies with rankings above threshold
high_performers = CompanyInfo.objects.filter(
    ranking__comprehensive_score__gte=80
).select_related('ranking')

# Find companies in specific industry chain
chain_companies = CompanyInfo.objects.filter(
    chain_points__chain_point__industry_chain__code='IC0076'
).distinct()

# Get financing history for company
company_funding = CompanyFinancing.objects.filter(
    company__keyno='COMPANY123'
).order_by('-financing_date')

# Geographic aggregation
city_stats = CompanyInfo.objects.values(
    'city'
).annotate(
    company_count=Count('keyno'),
    avg_score=Avg('ranking__comprehensive_score')
)
```

## Data Integrity and Validation

### Model Constraints
```python
# Unique constraints
keyno (CompanyInfo) - Primary key uniqueness
industry_chain.code - Unique chain codes
chain_point.code - Unique node codes

# Foreign key constraints  
CompanyRanking.company - OneToOne with CompanyInfo
CompanyFinancing.company - ForeignKey to CompanyInfo
ChainPoint.parent - Self-referencing hierarchy
```

### Custom Model Methods
```python
# CompanyRanking auto-calculation
def save(self):
    if not self.comprehensive_score:
        self.comprehensive_score = (sum of 5 dimensions) / 5
    super().save()

# Property methods for computed fields
@property
def company_count(self):  # On IndustryChain and ChainPoint
    return associated_companies.count()
```

## Database Optimization

### Indexes (Defined in Meta classes)
```python
# Performance indexes on frequently queried fields:
CompanyInfo: No explicit indexes (consider adding for industry, city)
CompanyFinancing: ['company'], ['financing_date'], ['financing_round']
IndustryChain: ['name'], ['code'] 
ChainPoint: ['level'], ['parent'], ['code']
Province/City/District: ['code'] with ordering
```

### Query Optimization Tips
```python
# Use select_related for foreign keys
companies = CompanyInfo.objects.select_related('ranking')

# Use prefetch_related for reverse foreign keys
chains = IndustryChain.objects.prefetch_related('chain_points__companies')

# Add database indexes for common filters
class Meta:
    indexes = [
        models.Index(fields=['industry', 'city']),
        models.Index(fields=['company_scale']),
    ]
```

